<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suhita</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1429">1429</a>–<a href="/years/1447">1447</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a> · Also known as Soheeta</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suhita was a Javanese queen regnant, the sixth monarch of the Majapahit empire, who ruled from 1429 until her death in 1447. She was the daughter of her predecessor, King Wikramawardhana, very probably by his principal wife Kusumawardhani; her two elder brothers died during their father's reign. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pararaton">Pararaton</a> records that the empire was ruled by a queen regnant after 1429, and Suhita is thought to have been that queen. She married her relative Prince Ratnapangkaja and was succeeded by her younger brother Dyah Kertawijaya. The Damarwulan legend of a maiden queen is associated with her reign, which saw a war with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/blambangan">Blambangan</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suhita.jpg" alt="Suhita" width="330" height="612" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Gunawan Kartapranata · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suhita.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Two queens reigned in their own right, Tribhuwana (1328–1350) and <b>Suhita</b> (1429–1447), the title Bhre was held by duchesses as well as dukes, and the Queen Grandmother Gayatri Rajapatni, a Buddhist nun, was revered as the “protector of the world” and deified after her death.</blockquote><a href="/societies/majapahit">Social Hierarchy of Majapahit</a></li></ul></section>
